# AGENTS.md — working with LLM-Lang canon

LLM-Lang compiles typed + documented code (JS/TS, C#) INTO compact canon
text (`~57%` of typed+documented sources on o200k, behavior identity held
down to Humanizer's 61,581-test vendored suite) and emits back OUT, round
trip stable. Canon's whole point is agents reading, authoring, and
repairing code — comments/doc-bloat drop by contract; executable
semantics ride through verbatim.

## Commands

```
ircc from-js file.ts  > file.ir     # JS/TS source → canon
ircc from-cs file.cs  > file.ir     # C# source → canon
ircc to-js file.ir    > file.js     # canon → JS emit (+ --map for a source map)
ircc to-cs file.ir    > file.cs     # canon → C# emit
ircc verify file.ir...              # canon-identity lint — RUN THIS, exit 1 on drift
ircc doc spec|tutorial|fidelity|versioning|skill|agents   # embedded docs
```

## Rules

1. **Canon identity**: every `.ir` file must be its own fixed point —
   `ircc verify` checks `file == print(expand(file))` and print→print
   stability; run it before proposing a change.
2. **Core forms are additive-only**: existing canon text never changes
   shape; growth lands as new rows (`ircc doc versioning`).
3. **Fidelity is budgeted with `opaque`**: constructs without a core form
   capture verbatim as `"opaque:…"` rows and re-emit byte-identically.
4. **Comments drop by contract**: machine canon never carries `//` rows.

## Canon rows (cheat sheet)

```
@1 @ns App.Billing
type Invoice export record{
  export ctor (id Long, total Decimal)
  export Bool Settled => Total >= 0
  export fn TryPost(acct String) Result<String,String>{…}
}
type Cache<T> : Object where T : class{ … }
fn Charge(amount Decimal, curr Currency = Currency.Usd) Bool{…}
var mut Balance = Money.Of(10.50m, Currency.Sek)
export get String Label { get; }
if a == b{ return 0 }
for x in items{ total += x }
mode switch{ Round.FLOOR => floor(mode), _ => bang }
try risky() catch NotFound return null finally Log()
return [.. items . Where(p => p.Active)]
```

Type words canonize capital (`String Int Bool Float Int64 ULong …`) and
map back to lowercase keywords on emit; other identifiers pass verbatim.

